/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (5.4 The Lagos Incident \(2016\))
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E ( The Lagos Attack was an Avengers operation carried out in Lagos, Nigeria, to capture Brock Rumlow, a former Hydra agent who attacked the IFID headquarters to steal a biological weapon. The mission, which escalated into open combat in the streets, ended in disaster when Rumlow attempted to kill Captain America with a suicide bomb in a crowded market. Wanda Maximoff, seeking to save Rogers and the civilians in the market, controlled the explosion and directed it toward a nearby building, but in doing so, accidentally caused the deaths of twenty-six civilians. As the Avengers were held responsible for this loss of life, the United Nations placed the Sokovia Accords on the agenda. Seeking to draw out the Avengers, Several international politicians, including Wakanda's ruler King T'Chaka, called for the United Nations to create a system of accountability. President Matthew Ellis held a press conference where he pledged his support in apprehending the people responsible. Secretary of State Thaddeus Ross brought the Avengers together and informed them that the United Nations was in the process of passing the Sokovia Accords, which would serve to monitor and police the increasing number of enhanced individuals.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
